  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Acting Now for Food Security and Resilient Food Systems - Mozambique</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">In this programme in Mozambique we support smallholder farmers to improve the production and productivity of grains, soy beans, maize, sorghum and fruits and vegetables. We aim to involve especially women and youth in providing inputs, technologies and services. Input and service providers are supported to provide accessible and affordable services to smallholders and their cooperatives or associations. Cooperatives and associations will play an essential role in enhancing smallholders&apos; positions, and we will support them to establish aggregation centres to collect and store their members&apos; produce. To avoid post-harvest losses, the programme sensitises smallholders through campaigns on how to process, preserve and properly store harvested produce. The Gender Action Learning System (GALS) methodology and the Engaging Men through Accountability Practice (EMAP) methodologies are two key strategies that are adopted to promote women&apos;s involvement in household decision-making.</narrative>
  </description>
